Version 3.58a:
- bugfixes (total 0);
- minor changes (total 1);
- VPA has been compiled with DOS Protected Mode Interface (DPMI). This allows
  using of all memory on your computer (not only the first 640k). The program
  now consists of a single VPA.EXE file (no more VPA.OVR), but requires two
  Borland DPMI files (RTM.EXE and DPMI16BI.OVL) to be present in the current
  directory or somewhere along the DOS PATH. Also, EMS memory is no longer
  used by VPA;
- VPA now stores Host Configuration messages in a text file named HCONFIG.TXT
  in the game directory (idea: S.Steblev);
- VPA can now produce TRN files! A TRN file (for the race you are playing) is
  created automatically by VPA and is updated each time you exit VPA after
  giving new orders to your empire. Also, if VPA detects a registered copy of
  WinPlan, then it produces a Version 3.5 TRN file. It is impossible to
  produce a Version 3.5 TRN file without WinPlan files. To use this feature,
  you must install VPA into the same directory as WinPlan or copy two files
  (namely REG.KEY and VPH35.DLL) from WinPlan to VPA directory (whatever is
  more convenient for you);
- VPA can now unpack RST files! When VPA detects a new RST file in the game
  directory, it asks if you want to unpack it. If you are playing in a team,
  you can bring your allies' RSTs later and VPA will detect and unpack them
  without re-unpacking your RST (or any RST that was unpacked earlier);
- additional information from Version 3.5 RST files is now used by VPA;
- TARGETn.EXT files are no longer used by VPA. These files were produced by
  VPUNPACK program to store more than 50 enemy target records. This feature
  is no longer needed as VPA can now obtain additional target records from
  Version 3.5 RST files and PHOST's UTILn.DAT files;

Version 3.58b:
- bugfixes (total 8);
- minor changes (total 1);
- new VPA.INI option: DeleteRST=Yes/No ([Interface] section, default is Yes).
  When this option is enabled, VPA deletes RST files after unpacking them,
  otherwise - leaves them in the game directory;

Version 3.58c:
- bugfixes (total 6);
- minor changes (total 14);
- UFO objects are now plotted on the map! They are represented by circles
  of the corresponding radii and colors on the screen. Detailed information on
  UFO objects can be displayed by clicking on their centers (also, Shift-Enter
  or Shift-Click will select the nearest circle-shaped object). UFO names are
  shown on the map next to them in high zoom modes (Shift-P toggles the
  visibility of planet and UFO names). You must be a registered WinPlan user
  to see UFO objects (this is Tim Wisseman's requirement);
- Shift-U key toggles UFO and wormhole visibility on the map. Shift-W is no
  longer used for this purpose;
- added "Fix" ("I") hot-key to the ship control screen. It is available for
  damaged or undermanned ships at starbases (idea: A.Bezborodov);
- 100% precise fuel burn calculation added! VPA now shows you how much fuel
  EXACTLY your ships burn when they move;
- 100% precise ship location calculation added! VPA now shows you EXACTLY where
  your ships end up after movement (except ships on Intercept, of course). If
  your ship is more than 1 move away from its waypoint, you can enter Distance
  Mode (right mouse button or spacebar), then press "N" to see the exact
  location of the ship on the next turn. This feature works with 100% precision
  only for Host 3.22.023 or better and PHOST 2.13 or better. Older Hosts had
  a couple of minor precision-defying glitches (thanks Tim for fixing them!);
- enemy ship movement prognosis added! You can now enter Distance Mode for
  enemy ships and see where they go and how much fuel they burn. If engine
  type of an enemy ship is unknown, VPA assumes it equal to its warp factor;
- new VPA.INI option: ScrambleShipNames=Yes/No ([Interface] section, default
  is No). When this option is enabled, VPA scrambles names of all your ships,
  so all other players see them as random codes like "Serial #12345678ABCD"
  (idea: D.Subbotin). This prevents other players from recognizing you by your
  personal ship naming style and from figuring out your map position by
  analysing ship explosion messages, that can be very useful when you don't
  want to be recognized by other players. Also, with this feature you can give
  meaningful names to your ships, like "$$$ 123 -> 456", without the risk of
  other players seeing them. It is recommended that you place the line
  "ScrambleShipNames = Yes" into the [Interface] section of local VPA.INI file
  in the directory of the game where you want your ship names scrambled, not
  into the main VPA.INI file, unless you want to scramble ship names in all
  of your games;
- screen saver added. After some time of inactivity VPA starts doing something
  on the screen ;)  New VPA.INI parameter "ScreenSaverTime=NNN" ([Interface]
  section, default is 5) defines the inactivity timeout in minutes. Zero value
  disables the screen saver;
- when ship's warp speed is set to 0, VPA no longer clears its waypoint. This
  is done for compatibility with certain add-ons;
- ship search function moved from F8 to Shift-F7 key;

Version 3.58d:
- bugfixes (total 0);
